{
  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "The current best (config_028, scvi_n200 + ViT + transformer + weighted, 0.725 acc) suggests scvi_n200 and multimodal fusion are both important, but we have never tested scvi_n200 with multiprofile in an RNA-only setting. The gap between config_007 (pca, RNA-only, singleprofile: 0.485) and config_020 (scvi, multimodal, multiprofile: 0.706) conflates three changes simultaneously (encoder, profile, modality). Config_032 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) cleanly isolates how much of the 0.706 performance comes from the RNA representation and multiprofile aggregation alone versus the image modality. If RNA-only scvi approaches ~0.65+, the image contribution is modest and future effort should focus on RNA representation; if it stays near ~0.50–0.55, the multimodal combination is genuinely additive and justifies further multimodal exploration. This is the highest-information experiment under the limited budget because it resolves a critical uncertainty that will determine whether to exploit the multimodal direction further or pivot toward simpler RNA-centric designs."
}

